			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the single character defined exclusively by <Picture 1>. All views in the character sheet depict the same individual. The picture supplies character identity and design only, not the target composition or action.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] A ten-second photorealistic scene shows <Subject 1> gathering loose hair, securing it into a ponytail, adjusting a loose strand, and looking toward the camera with a small, satisfied smile.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears throughout [Shot 1]): partially_preserved. Preserve the reference character's identity and complete outfit. Allow only the hairstyle to change naturally from loose hair to a secured ponytail through visible hand actions. Preserve the reference hair length, color, and volume. Do not reproduce the character-sheet background, labels, grid, or multiple figures.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action cinematography in a quiet, sunlit room beside a window. Soft side light and gentle fill keep the face, hands, and individual hair strands clearly readable. Natural skin texture and restrained cinematic color.\n\n[Shot 1] One continuous ten-second shot. Use an eye-level, waist-up three-quarter frontal composition, leaving enough space above and beside the head to contain both raised elbows and all hand movements. A single elastic hair tie is initially around the right wrist. The camera makes a very slow, subtle push inward without cropping the hands.\n\nFrom 00:00 to 00:02.000, <Subject 1> raises both hands and sweeps the loose hair backward from either side of the head. Fingers visibly pass through and guide the hair. The head tilts slightly forward as the hands move toward the back of the head.\n\nFrom 00:02.000 to 00:04.000, the left hand gathers and holds the hair together behind the head while the right hand smooths the remaining loose sections into the same bundle. Hair follows the hands with believable drag and settles under gravity. Keep the face recognizable between the moving arms.\n\nFrom 00:04.000 to 00:07.000, the left hand maintains its grip on the gathered hair. The right hand takes the elastic from the wrist, stretches it around the bundle, and works with the left hand to secure the ponytail. Keep the gathering and fastening process continuous and physically coherent. The hairstyle changes progressively through contact; it must not transform instantly while the hands merely hover nearby.\n\nFrom 00:07.000 to 00:08.500, <Subject 1> releases the secured ponytail and lowers both arms. The ponytail drops and sways briefly with natural weight, remaining visibly attached at the fastening point. One hand gently adjusts a loose strand beside the face, then lowers.\n\nFrom 00:08.500 to 00:10.000, <Subject 1> lifts the chin slightly, looks toward the camera, and gives a small, relaxed smile. A subtle head turn makes the secured ponytail visible beside the head. Hold the completed hairstyle through the final moment.\n\nExactly one person and one hair tie. Normal real-time movement throughout. No slow motion, cuts, mirrors, duplicated hands, fused fingers, hair passing through the body, floating hair, sudden changes in hair length, identity drift, outfit changes, subtitles, logos, or watermarks.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nQuiet indoor room tone, faint outdoor birds through the window, gentle clothing movement, and subtle hair-handling sounds. No dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nNone."
